    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A beautifully presented 3-bedroom detached bungalow on c. 0.69 acre site set in the peaceful countryside of Cousinstown, Bridgetown, Co. Wexford. This impressive home offers bright, spacious accommodation with an excellent flow throughout, creating a warm and welcoming atmosphere from the moment you enter. At the heart of the property is a stunning sunroom, flooded with natural light and featuring a sunny aspect and impressive vaulted ceilings. This exceptional space provides the perfect setting for relaxing, entertaining, or simply enjoying views of the surrounding gardens. The well-designed layout combines practicality and style, with generous living accommodation ideally suited to modern family living. Further benefits include an attached garage offering excellent storage and potential for a variety of uses, ample off-street parking, and mature gardens that provide a wonderful outdoor environment for family life or peaceful country living. Conveniently located, the property is just a short drive from the villages of Bridgetown and Kilmore, where a range of everyday amenities can be found, including shops, schools, churches, pharmacies, and sporting facilities. The picturesque fishing village of Kilmore Quay is also nearby, offering a beautiful marina, renowned seafood restaurants, and seasonal boat trips to the stunning Saltee Islands. The area is further enhanced by an abundance of nearby sandy beaches, including Carne, St. Helens, Rosslare Strand, and Rosslare Harbour, making it an ideal location for those who enjoy coastal living and outdoor pursuits. Wexford Town is approximately 17km away, while excellent connectivity to the N25, M11, and national road network ensures easy access to Dublin City and Dublin Airport in under 2.5 hours. This is a rare opportunity to acquire a truly special home in one of County Wexford’s most sought-after and scenic locations. Viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation Comprises:\r\nEntrance Porch – (2.25m x 2.01m), Tiled floor, double doors opening onto entrance hall.\r\nEntrance Hall – (5.35m x 2.24m), Tiled floor, coving, large walk in hot press.\r\nMaster Bedroom – (3.63m x 3.63m),  Carpet flooring, Bay window, walk in wardrobe.\r\nEn-Suite – (1.71m x 1.45m),  WC, WHB, Electric shower, tiled flooring and part tiled walls.\r\nBedroom No.2 – (4.25m x 3.02m),  Carpet flooring, Bay window.\r\nBedroom No. 3 – (3.99m x 2.77m),  Carpet flooring, Bay window.\r\nLiving Room – (6.12m x 3.69m),  Wooden flooring, cast iron fireplace, coving, centre rose, TV point, Bay window, double doors to sunroom.\r\nSun Room – (4.88m x 4.59m),  Tiled flooring, double doors to living room and french doors to patio area, high ceiling with centre rose, archway into\r\nKitchen/Dining area.\r\nKitchen/Dining area – (6.12m x 5.18m),  Eye & Waist level units, tiled flooring & splashback, oven & hob with extractor fan, recessed lighting.\r\nUtility Room – (2.77m x 1.84m),  Eye & Waist level units, tiled flooring & splashback, door to side of house.\r\nBathroom – (3.38m x 2.16m),  WC, WHB, tiled flooring, part tiled walls, bath, shower.\r\nGarage – (6.10m x 3.65m),  Concrete floor, double doors to the front, oil burner, stire to attic.\r\n\r\nOutside: Mature garden to rear with patio & pergola, garage which is attached to the house but not accessible from the house.\r\nServices: Electricity, mains water, septic tank, oil fired central heating.\r\nBER: E Ber No: 119482578 Performance indicator: 286.64 kWh/m2/yr\r\nApply: Keane Auctioneers (053) 9123072"
      },
